[38;5;231m⏺[39m Last question. This one's about the module's interface — the part other code will be written against, so it's the
  expensive one to change later.

  [1mThe fork:[0m what a caller asks the settings module for.

  - [1mFull URLs per endpoint[0m — settings exposes [38;5;153mloginUrl[39m directly. Mirrors today's [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m exactly and is the
    smallest possible move. Cost: every future endpoint repeats the host in every environment, so a host change is an
    N×M edit.
  - [1mBase URL plus paths[0m — settings exposes [38;5;153mapiBaseUrl[39m, and callers join it with a path (or the module exposes a small
    [38;5;153mendpoints[39m map built from the base). Adding an endpoint touches one place and a host change touches one line per
    environment. Cost: marginally more structure than one stub call strictly needs today.

  With exactly one endpoint in the repo these are nearly identical in size, so the choice is really about which shape
  you want to be living with at endpoint three or four. I'd take [1mbase URL plus paths[0m — it's what makes "easier to change
  environments" actually hold as the app grows, and it's the reason to build a settings module rather than move a
  constant.

  On the environment list: unless you say otherwise I'll assume [1mlocal development plus production[0m, with
  [38;5;153mlocalhost[39m/[38;5;153m127.0.0.1[39m mapping to dev and everything else falling back to production — and I'll record the specific
  dev/staging hostnames as an assumption to validate rather than invent them. Tell me your real hostnames and I'll wire
  them in directly.
